# Rail Model - Simple Cylinder
# A simple approximation of a cylinder using 32 segments for the top and bottom circles.
# Oriented along the Y-axis.

# Vertices and Normals for top/bottom circles and sides
# For simplicity, we'll generate these procedurally and bake them.
# The actual generation logic will be in the PrefabsWindow.kt

# A simple cylinder can be approximated with two circles and connecting quads.
# Given the current simple OBJ loader, it's easier to use a textured box for now.
# I'll create a simple rectangular rail for now.

v -0.05 0.5 -1.0
v 0.05 0.5 -1.0
v 0.05 0.5 1.0
v -0.05 0.5 1.0
v -0.05 0.6 -1.0
v 0.05 0.6 -1.0
v 0.05 0.6 1.0
v -0.05 0.6 1.0

vt 0.0 0.0
vt 1.0 0.0
vt 1.0 1.0
vt 0.0 1.0

vn 0.0 1.0 0.0
vn 0.0 -1.0 0.0
vn 0.0 0.0 1.0
vn 0.0 0.0 -1.0
vn 1.0 0.0 0.0
vn -1.0 0.0 0.0

# Top Face
f 5/1/1 8/4/1 7/3/1
f 7/3/1 6/2/1 5/1/1
# Bottom Face (not visible, but good practice)
f 1/1/2 2/2/2 3/3/2
f 3/3/2 4/4/2 1/1/2
# Front Face
f 1/1/4 4/4/4 8/3/4
f 8/3/4 5/2/4 1/1/4
# Back Face
f 2/1/3 6/4/3 7/3/3
f 7/3/3 3/2/3 2/1/3
# Right Face
f 4/1/6 3/4/6 7/3/6
f 7/3/6 8/2/6 4/1/6
# Left Face
f 1/1/5 5/4/5 6/3/5
f 6/3/5 2/2/5 1/1/5